"""
Time-series temperature applied to a `HeatPort`.

Ported from `ShipSIM.Components.Others.HeatTransfer.TemperatureDataset`.

The original Modelica model wired:
- `Modelica.Blocks.Tables.CombiTable1D(fileName=…, tableName=…, tableOnFile=true)` reading
  a (sec, K) table from a .txt file, with `time` as input.
- `Modelica.Thermal.HeatTransfer.Sources.PrescribedTemperature` consuming the table
  output and exposing a `HeatPort_b`.

The Dyad port composes the same pipeline using:
- `BlockComponents.Tables.Interpolation` reading a `DyadData.DyadTimeseries` (CSV) — the
  `dataset` parameter is the only structural parameter; the rest is data-driven.
- `ThermalComponents.Sources.PrescribedTemperature` translating the interpolated value
  to a `HeatPort` (with the standard built-in `HeatPort` connector).

The default dataset path is `dyad://DyadShip/temperature_24h.csv` (a 24-hour synthetic
temperature swing in `assets/`). Users with a longer or differently-named dataset can
override the `dataset` structural parameter at the call site.

The original's `tableOnFile = true` always-load-from-disk behaviour is replaced by
`DyadData`'s URI-based loader. Linear interpolation between rows + boundary-value
extrapolation outside the data range is hard-coded to match the upstream
`HoldLastPoint` behaviour.
"""
component TemperatureDataset
  "Time-series of (time [s], temperature [K]) — defaults to the bundled 24-h sample."
  structural parameter dataset::DyadData.DyadTimeseries = DyadData.DyadTimeseries(
    "dyad://DyadShip/temperature_24h.csv",
    independent_var = "time",
    dependent_vars = ["T"]
  )

  port_AirTemp = HeatPort()

  TemperatureData = BlockComponents.Tables.Interpolation(
    interpolation_type = BlockComponents.Tables.InterpolationType.LinearInterpolation(),
    extrapolation_type = BlockComponents.Tables.ExtrapolationType.Constant(),
    dataset = dataset
  )

  prescribedTemperature = ThermalComponents.Sources.PrescribedTemperature()
relations
  TemperatureData.u = time
  connect(TemperatureData.y, prescribedTemperature.T)
  connect(prescribedTemperature.port, port_AirTemp)
end
